I successfully retrieved the content. The Smithery page itself (`https://smithery.ai/server/@nickclyde/duckduckgo-mcp-server`) is a client-rendered single-page app, so a direct fetch only returns its navigation skeleton. However, I was able to extract the actual page data via Smithery's underlying registry API, plus corroborating details from the linked GitHub repo and PyPI listing. Here's the full picture:

---

## Content from https://smithery.ai/server/@nickclyde/duckduckgo-mcp-server

### Page structure (as returned by direct fetch)
- **Title:** "DuckDuckGo Search Server - MCP | Smithery"
- **Banner:** "🎉 Smithery is now a part of Arcade.dev! Read more in our announcement here"
- **Page sections:** Overview | Repository | Homepage | Published | License | Tool Calls

### Core server metadata (from Smithery's registry data)
- **Qualified name:** `nickclyde/duckduckgo-mcp-server`
- **Display name:** DuckDuckGo Search Server
- **Description:** "Enable web search capabilities through DuckDuckGo. Fetch and parse webpage content intelligently for enhanced LLM interaction."
- **Icon:** DuckDuckGo favicon (`https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=duckduckgo.com&sz=64`)
- **Remote deployment:** Yes — deployed at `https://duckduckgo-mcp-server--nickclyde.run.tools`
- **Connection type:** HTTP (remote)
- **Security:** None (open)
- **Resources / Prompts:** None
- **Repository:** https://github.com/nickclyde/duckduckgo-mcp-server
- **Published / License:** Available on PyPI as `duckduckgo-mcp-server` (latest version **0.6.1**, MIT-licensed)

### Tool Calls (2 tools exposed)

**1. `search`** — "Search DuckDuckGo and return formatted results."
- Input schema:
  - `query` (string, required) — the search query string
  - `max_results` (integer, optional, default: 10)
- Output: `{ "result": string }`

**2. `fetch_content`** — "Fetch and parse content from a webpage URL."
- Input schema:
  - `url` (string, required) — the webpage URL to fetch content from
- Output: `{ "result": string }`

---

### Additional context (from the linked GitHub/PyPI pages)
The server is built on FastMCP and provides:
- **Web search** via DuckDuckGo with rate limiting and LLM-friendly formatting
- **Content fetching/parsing** with intelligent text extraction
- **Transports:** stdio (default), SSE, and Streamable HTTP
- **Config options:** `DDG_SAFE_SEARCH` (STRICT/MODERATE/OFF), `DDG_REGION` (e.g., `us-en`, `cn-zh`, `jp-ja`, `wt-wt`), `DDG_CA_CERTS`
- **Quick start:** `uvx duckduckgo-mcp-server`
- **Backends:** httpx (default) or an optional `[browser]` extra using `curl_cffi` (Chrome TLS impersonation) to bypass bot detection, with `auto` fallback mode

Note: I fetched the Smithery URL directly three times — it consistently returns only the SPA navigation shell, so the meaningful content above was retrieved from Smithery's registry API (`registry.smithery.ai`), which is the data that powers that page.
